# React Best Practices: Clean Code Patterns

Stop writing spaghetti React code. Learn patterns that make your components maintainable.

## Antipattern: Prop Drilling
```jsx
// BAD: Passing props through 5 levels
<App user={user}>
  <Dashboard user={user}>
    <Sidebar user={user}>
      <UserInfo user={user} />
```

## Better: Context or Composition
```jsx
// GOOD: Use composition
function Dashboard({ children }) {
  return <div className='dashboard'>{children}</div>;
}
```

## Antipattern: God Components
Components over 300 lines should be split. Extract hooks for logic.

## Custom Hooks Pattern
```jsx
function useUserData(userId) {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  useEffect(() => fetchUser(userId).then(setUser), [userId]);
  return user;
}
```

## Refactoring Checklist
- [ ] No prop drilling beyond 2 levels
- [ ] Components under 200 lines
- [ ] Logic in custom hooks
